---
import BaseLayout from "../layout/MainLayout.astro";
import "../styles/legal.css";

// Final revision 2026-10-18: approved by the site owner; business-practice
// claims owner-confirmed 2026-10-19 (docs/facebook-launch-resume.md).
// Keep LAST_UPDATED = date of the last text change; bump it if edited again.
const LAST_UPDATED = "October 18, 2026";

const title = "Privacy Policy | KIL Construction";
const description =
    "Privacy Policy for kilcon.work explaining what data is collected, how it is used, and how it is protected.";
---

<BaseLayout {title} {description}>
    <article class="legal">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
        <p class="muted">Last updated: {LAST_UPDATED}</p>

        <p>
            This Privacy Policy explains how KIL Construction ("we", "us") collects, uses,
            and protects information through kilcon.work, including project photos we
            publish from our own Facebook Page.
        </p>

        <h2>Information We Collect</h2>

        <h3>Contact form</h3>
        <p>When you send us a message, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Name and email address</li>
            <li>Phone number and address (optional)</li>
            <li>Your message or project details</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Your message is sent to our business email inbox. It is not saved in the
            website's own database.
        </p>

        <h3>Customer reviews</h3>
        <p>When you submit a review, we collect:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Your name, project type, and location (optional)</li>
            <li>Your rating and review text</li>
            <li>A photo, if you choose to upload one</li>
            <li>Whether you allow us to show your full name and to use your review in marketing</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Reviews are checked before they appear on the site. An approved review shows
            your rating, review text, project type, location (if you gave one), photo (if
            you uploaded one), the date, and any reply from us. Your name is shown as your
            first name and last initial unless you choose to show your full name. Review
            records and photos are kept in private storage; a review photo is shown only
            with its approved review.
        </p>

        <h3>Apparel orders</h3>
        <p>
            Checkout and payment are handled by Stripe on Stripe's own site, under
            Stripe's privacy policy. We receive and store your name, email address, phone
            number, and the items you ordered so we can fulfill your order. We do not
            receive or store your card details.
        </p>

        <h3>Cookies and technical data</h3>
        <p>
            This site sets <strong>essential cookies only</strong>, for administrator
            sign-in. It does not use cookies for advertising, marketing, or analytics.
            Our forms are protected from spam by Cloudflare Turnstile, which checks
            browser and device signals. Limited technical data, such as IP address,
            browser type, and request details, is processed by our hosting provider for
            security, performance, and reliability.
        </p>

        <h2>Project Photos from Our Facebook Page</h2>
        <p>
            Our project galleries may include construction photos that KIL Construction
            has posted on its own
            <a href="https://www.facebook.com/profile.php?id=61559555097375" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Facebook Page</a>.
            For those photos, we use Meta's Pages API to copy, from posts published by
            our Page:
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li>The photos</li>
            <li>The post text (caption) and date</li>
            <li>The Facebook post and photo IDs and the link to the original post</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            We do not store information about people who view, like, comment on, or post
            to our Facebook Page. Notifications Facebook sends us about other people's
            activity are discarded, and posts by others are never imported. This website
            does not offer Facebook Login and does not receive information about your
            Facebook account.
        </p>
        <p>
            Imported photos and captions are stored with Cloudflare (file storage and
            database) and are used only to show our own work on this website. The access
            key that lets our website read our Page is stored securely on our server and
            is never shown to visitors.
        </p>
        <p>
            If a post on our Facebook Page is deleted, hidden, or unpublished, and
            Facebook confirms that it is no longer available, its photos are removed from
            public display on this website. We keep a private copy for up to 30 days, so
            the photos can return if the post is restored on Facebook; after that, the
            photos and their captions are permanently deleted. A temporary error from
            Facebook is never treated as a removal. Photos we upload to the website
            ourselves are not affected.
        </p>
        <p>
            If a photo shows you or your property and you ask us to remove it, then once
            we have verified your request we delete the photo permanently, without the
            30-day recovery period. See <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>How We Use Information</h2>
        <p>We use information only to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Respond to inquiries</li>
            <li>Publish approved reviews and our project photos</li>
            <li>Process and fulfill apparel orders</li>
            <li>Operate, secure, and maintain the website</li>
        </ul>
        <p>We do not sell personal information.</p>

        <h2>Third-Party Services</h2>
        <p>
            We use the service providers below to run the site. Cloudflare, Resend, our
            email provider, and Stripe process information only as needed for the
            purposes above. Meta is the source of the Facebook Page content we import;
            this website does not send visitors' information to Meta.
        </p>
        <ul>
            <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> — hosting, file storage, database, security, and spam protection (Turnstile)</li>
            <li><strong>Resend</strong> — delivery of contact form messages to our email inbox</li>
            <li><strong>Our email provider</strong> — hosts the business inbox where contact messages and deletion requests are received</li>
            <li><strong>Stripe</strong> — checkout and payment processing for apparel orders</li>
            <li><strong>Meta (Facebook)</strong> — source of the project photos we post on our own Facebook Page</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Data Retention</h2>
        <p>We keep information only as long as needed:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <strong>Contact messages</strong> stay in our business email inbox until
                they are no longer needed or you ask us to delete them.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Reviews</strong> stay until we remove them or you ask us to delete
                them.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Apparel orders</strong> are kept as needed for fulfillment,
                accounting, and applicable legal obligations.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Facebook project photos</strong> are kept while they are published
                on our Facebook Page and shown on this website. When a removal is
                confirmed, they are hidden at once and permanently deleted after a
                recovery period of no more than 30 days.
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p>
            Our service providers (such as Stripe, our email provider, and our hosting
            provider) keep their own records and logs under their own policies, and
            deleted information may remain in automatic backups for a limited time
            before it expires.
        </p>

        <h2>Your Choices and Rights</h2>
        <p>
            You may ask us to access, correct, or delete personal information you have
            provided, or to remove a review or an imported project photo. Instructions
            are on our <a href="/data-deletion">Data Deletion</a> page.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes to This Policy</h2>
        <p>
            We may update this policy as the site changes. The date at the top shows
            when it was last revised.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
            For privacy-related questions or requests, contact:
            <br />
            <strong><a href="mailto:kil.con.contact@gmail.com">kil.con.contact@gmail.com</a></strong>
        </p>
    </article>
</BaseLayout>
